## CQ-CC13-01 | config watcher: edit a Common config file while the game runs, the change loads without a restart
@group client
@commands Full pack client in a world: open `config/creativecommon-common.toml`, change a value with a visible effect (for example an `[effects] levelCaps` entry or `[melting] meltTickInterval`), save; read `logs/latest.log`
@pass log shows the watcher noticing the file and the Forge reload path running once after the 1 s debounce; the new value is in effect without a restart; saving unchanged content does not reload
@fails `OwnConfigLogic` file filter, debounce, content guard
@reviewed 2026-11-24
# steps written r1124gate 2026-11-24 (runner-4): single-player full-pack capture client (`run_captures.py serve`, the run's usual unlisted-jar --drop set), flat creative world
bootexpect \[creativecommon\] config watcher on: [0-9]+ own config file
bootreject config watcher could not start
> effect clear @s
> effect give @s minecraft:luck 60 2
do {"effects": true, "expect": "minecraft:luck amp 2"}
shell sed -i 's/^\([[:space:]]*levelCaps = \[\)/\1"minecraft:luck=1", /' config/creativecommon-common.toml; test "$(grep -c '"minecraft:luck=1"' config/creativecommon-common.toml)" = 1
waitlog \[creativecommon\] creativecommon-common\.toml reloaded 20
> effect clear @s
> effect give @s minecraft:luck 60 2
do {"effects": true, "expect": "minecraft:luck amp 0"}
shell python3 -c "p='config/creativecommon-common.toml'; d=open(p,'rb').read(); open(p,'wb').write(d)"
sleep 5
shell sed -i 's/"minecraft:luck=1", //' config/creativecommon-common.toml
waitlog \[creativecommon\] creativecommon-common\.toml reloaded 20
> effect clear @s
> effect give @s minecraft:luck 60 2
do {"effects": true, "expect": "minecraft:luck amp 2"}
count \[creativecommon\] creativecommon-common\.toml reloaded == 2
reject reloading creativecommon-common\.toml failed|config watcher pass failed
look the first reload line lands about 1 s after the edit (log timestamps against the shell step); the unchanged rewrite gave no reload (count 2: the edit and the revert)
## CQ-CC13-02 | melt and salt tooltip: salt and saltable blocks show the melting hint
@group client
@commands Full pack client: hover a salt item, an ice block and a snow block in the inventory
@pass the saltable tooltip line shows on the blocks salt melts; Salt (the salt dust) and Salt Melt show a gray "Usable on ice and snow" line; no tooltip line on blocks it does not melt; The Salt's merged salt (`salt:salt`) shows the removed-item line (it merges into the salt dust, item_merges.md 2.9)
@fails saltable tag, item tag `creativecompat:melting/salt_items` (`melting_tags.js`, key `i.t_melt_salt_items` in Common's item_dict.js), tooltip handler (`SaltableTooltip` in Creative Compat's `melting/`), Compat lang keys `creativecompat.tooltip.saltable`, `creativecompat.tooltip.salt_use`
@reviewed 2026-11-24
@jars creativecompat creativecommon
@sources development/creativeCompat/src/main/java/com/SaintAlfonzo/creativecompat/melting/SaltableTooltip.java
# 2026-11-25 (creative-common-publish #22, #23): salt items get the "Usable on ice and snow" line; the standard salt is `vintagedelight:salt_dust`, `salt:salt` is the merged duplicate (removed-item line expected)
# retargeted 2026-11-24 (r1124gate ruling): melting and the Saltable tooltip moved to Creative Compat in the wave 2 carve, so the row tests the Compat jar, not the Common 1.3.0 gate
# steps written r1124gate 2026-11-24 (runner-4): single-player full-pack capture client (`run_captures.py serve`, the run's usual unlisted-jar --drop set), flat creative world
