## SQ-CC13-09 | Wither Immunity: Wither is refused while it lasts, and an existing Wither deals no damage
@group A (full pack)
@commands bot in survival: `/effect give BOT minecraft:wither 20 1`, wait 2 s, `/effect give BOT creativecommon:wither_immunity 30`, read health over 5 s; `/effect clear BOT minecraft:wither`, `/effect give BOT minecraft:wither 10`; `/data get entity BOT ActiveEffects`
@pass health stops falling once the immunity is on; the second Wither give fails (`Unable to apply this effect`) and no Wither is in ActiveEffects; JEI and JEED show the name Wither Immunity and its description
@fails `effect/WitherImmunityEffect` not registered on the event bus; `effects/wither_immunity.js` (the effect id missing)
@reviewed 2026-11-26
@absent creativecommon:wither_immunity (effect registered by KubeJS startup script, not in the last /dumpall)
# written 2026-11-26 (r1126q writer-5): bots are invulnerable (Bots.java), so a NoAI pillager "qp" on Normal takes the Wither (as SQ-EFX-02); Wither ticks are DamageSource.WITHER, canceled while the immunity is on
> execute unless entity qe run pbot spawn qe -50 -60 -50 minecraft:overworld survival
sleep 3
> difficulty normal
> execute as @e[type=minecraft:pillager] run kill @s
> summon minecraft:pillager -46 -60 -46 {NoAI:1b,PersistenceRequired:1b,Tags:["qp"]}
sleep 1
> cdevtest reg effect creativecommon:wither_immunity
> effect give @e[tag=qp,limit=1] minecraft:wither 20 1
sleep 2
> data get entity @e[tag=qp,limit=1] Health
capture H1 has the following entity data: ([0-9.]+)f
> effect give @e[tag=qp,limit=1] creativecommon:wither_immunity 30
> data get entity @e[tag=qp,limit=1] Health
capture H2 has the following entity data: ([0-9.]+)f
sleep 5
> data get entity @e[tag=qp,limit=1] Health
capture H3 has the following entity data: ([0-9.]+)f
shell python3 -c "import sys; print('wither health', {H1}, {H2}, {H3}); sys.exit(0 if {H1} < 24 and {H3} == {H2} else 1)"
> effect clear @e[tag=qp,limit=1] minecraft:wither
> effect give @e[tag=qp,limit=1] minecraft:wither 10
waitlog Unable to apply this effect 10
> execute unless entity @e[tag=qp,nbt={ActiveEffects:[{Id:20b}]}] run say CC13-09 no wither on the target
expect CC13-09 no wither on the target
expect verb=reg kind=effect .*creativecommon:wither_immunity
reject \[cdevtest\] .*done=0
> execute as @e[tag=qp] run kill @s
## SQ-CC13-10 | own config watcher: only stamped jars are taken over from Forge
@group A (full pack)
@commands boot; grep latest.log for the config watcher start line; edit `config/creativecompat-common.toml` and a third-party config (`config/quark-common.toml`) while running
@pass the Creative config reloads once after about 1 s (Common's watcher); the third-party file follows Forge's own watcher; no `config watcher could not start`
@fails `OwnConfigWatcher.stamped` (the `META-INF/ce-build.json` lookup) for nested or bundled jars
@reviewed 2026-11-26
# written 2026-11-26 (r1126q writer-5): the log line is the one CQ-CC13-01 reads; a comment appended to a toml is a content change (the watcher's loop guard compares content)
bootexpect \[creativecommon\] config watcher on: [0-9]+ own config file
bootreject config watcher could not start
shell test -f config/creativecompat-common.toml && test -f config/quark-common.toml
shell printf '\n# cc13-10 watcher probe\n' >> config/creativecompat-common.toml
waitlog \[creativecommon\] creativecompat-common\.toml reloaded 20
shell printf '\n# cc13-10 watcher probe\n' >> config/quark-common.toml
sleep 6
count \[creativecommon\] creativecompat-common\.toml reloaded == 1
reject \[creativecommon\] quark-common\.toml reloaded
reject reloading creativecompat-common\.toml failed|config watcher pass failed
